Z||000000||PAUL88GT||10-20-1999||06:19 PM||||I just purchased an 88GT and I also own an 86 2M4.  Can anyone recommend a good, low cost repair manual for the 88GT? If so, where can it be purchased?<P>TIA||||reg||5
Z||000001||mwbackus||10-21-1999||05:04 AM||||The 88 GM shop manual is hard to find and seems to command a very high price (ie.over $80).  One could almost suspect that sooner or later someone will scan the entire thing, and try to sell the files on the net.  But not me! I really hate copyright lawyers, fines, and other related yucky things.  Both the Chiltons and Haynes manuals are avail. at most discount auto stores and they are quite inexpensive, but, they do not even come close to the indepth info provided by the shop manual.<P>Mike||||reg||1
Z||000002||Thomas||10-21-1999||05:31 AM||||A good low price Manuel:<BR>Haynes Book <BR>An expensive but i find the best is the original service manuel from GM.<BR>An additional Manuel are the CDs from ALLDATA.<BR>For $ 29,95 you get the CDs and a free registration for one Car and Engine. Every next car and engine cost $ 9,95 for registration.<BR>The most pictures on this CDs are a copy from Original GM Manuels. But the best at this CDs are the Service Bulletins from GM.<BR>With the Bulletins you can find many ways to fix for non documendet Problems.<BR>exemble: Some Fiero Owner in Germany have the Problem with the transaxle seals in the gear. Some months after renewing the seals, they begin to leak again.<BR>Service bulletin says: Use a Plastic tool for installing the axle or you damaged the seal with the axle. ( special the right side)<BR>I never found this tool in any other manuels.<P>I don´t like the Chilton repair manuel. Its to small with Information for my Fiero.||||reg||1
Z||000003||ka4nkf||10-21-1999||09:51 AM||||I Saw A 88 GM Manual On E-Bay. I Think The Highest Bid Was $40.00 . Very Good Price||||reg||1
Z||000004||PAUL88GT||10-21-1999||12:22 PM||||Thanks for the info.  I will check out the GM shop manual on e-bay.<P>Has anyone used this ALLDATA CD? If so, was is useful?||||reg||7
Z||000005||Thomas||10-22-1999||01:56 AM||||Look at this side and you find a list of all Service Bulletins for Fieros include the 88 V6. <BR>I live in Germany and here you can´t find info over the Bulletins.<BR>Maybe in US it is not so. I don´t know.<BR>For me is the Alldata CD a good Databank with all infos i need in additional to the other books.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.alldata.com/consumer/TSB/48/88481211.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.alldata.com/consumer/TSB/48/88481211.html</A> ||||reg||14
Z||000006||RossT||10-22-1999||02:47 AM||||The chiltons manual was re-written in<BR>1997 with much more detail, over 300 pages.  It is now called "General Motors<BR>Fiero 1984-1988" It is a vast improvement<BR>over the original chilton and haynes, both<BR>are not very good.   I just placed an<BR>order for the updated version on Amazon.com.  I also have the 88 factory<BR>service manual, and sometimes find it<BR>to be way over my novice capabilities.<P><BR>Ross||||reg||1
Z||000007||DJRice||10-22-1999||09:36 AM||||I have the Alldata CD for my Fiero, and I like it.  Its been pretty helpful.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Standard||10-25-1999||03:02 AM||||I have both the Chilton's and the Hayne's manuals.  I like the Hayne's manual because it's organized very good, although it is pretty basic.  The Chiltons goes more in depth on some things and has lots more info about the body, but seems (to me) more disorganized than the Haynes.  imho<BR>||||reg||1
